# Trial of the Soul with a test bot. The bot can't fight, so each wave is killed by command. Waves spawn
# 3 s after the start; the watcher checks once a second and sends the next wave as soon as one is cleared.
# Expect: step=trial while running, the log shows waves 1-3, then step=race with ttl.trial.passed=true,
# then step=unique with three ttl.uniqueOptions from the "knowledge" pool.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotTrial
@sleep 2
kill TtlBotTrial
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl trial
ttl inspect TtlBotTrial
@sleep 5
kill @e[tag=ttl_trial]
@sleep 3
kill @e[tag=ttl_trial]
@sleep 3
kill @e[tag=ttl_trial]
@sleep 3
ttl inspect TtlBotTrial
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl choose slime
ttl inspect TtlBotTrial
# Not an option (great_sage is Legendary): must be refused, the bot stays at step=unique.
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl unique great_sage
# The 3 options are random; try the whole knowledge pool, only the first offered one goes through.
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl unique analyst
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl unique researcher
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl unique mathematician
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl unique observer
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl unique seer
execute as TtlBotTrial run ttl unique seeker
ttl inspect TtlBotTrial
ttl registry
ttl reset TtlBotTrial
ttlbot remove TtlBotTrial
